_kin': "Exodus 23:20-33 (exo_23_escort_land — eight Onkelos rows), 34:11-16 (exo_34_second_tablets — seven), Numbers 33:50-56 (num_33_journeys — seven), the Mekhilta's twenty-one rows — credited by name at the reading"}; the_calfs_agency = Avodah Zarah 53b:7-11 (opened whole): THE SHELF'S THEORY OF THE DEMOLITION COMMAND — the Land is Israel's inheritance from the fathers and a person cannot forbid what is not his, so the gentiles could not have forbidden its trees; but since Israel worshipped the calf ('these are your GODS' — plural, many gods desired) the gentiles who worshipped were ISRAEL'S AGENTS: the Asherim a Jew's idols, irrevocable, hence BURNED rather than revoked (12:3; 7:5); which Asherim? who can tell — all forbidden; so the brick: a Jew's intent revealed, the gentile his agent; the_bans_condition = {'repentance': "Sotah 35b:10 (opened whole) — R. Shimon: the law written ON the plaster and 'lest they teach you to do like all their abominations' (20:18) written BELOW for the nations to read: had the inhabitants REPENTED, Israel would have accepted them", 'outside_the_land': "Sotah 35b:13, 36a:1 — 'when you go forth to battle … and take them captive' (21:10) includes even Canaanites OUTSIDE THE LAND: if they repent they are accepted; 'you shall keep alive none that breathes' (20:16) is not of those outside the Land (R. Shimon — the reason 20:18 read)"}; the_pitys_row = {'shelf_rows_citing_7_16_for_the_pity': 0, 'the_one_row_on_7_16': "Bava Kamma 113b:7 — on 'consume': robbing a gentile prohibited, the peoples' property consumed only when delivered into your hand", 'the_seats_forward': ['Deut 13:9', 'Deut 19:13', 'Deut 19:21', 'Deut 25:12', 'Deut 7:16']} (the other settings recorded in DATA)

